          <h3>ALMA CO Absorption in Active Galaxies</h3>
          <p class="meta">
            Brigham Young University · Advisor: Dr. Benjamin Boizelle · Summer 2025–Present
          </p>
          <p>
            Archival ALMA study of carbon monoxide absorption lines against bright radio cores in active
            galaxies. This project uses spectral extraction, continuum fitting, Gaussian modeling, and
            molecular column-density estimates to characterize cold gas near AGN. The project is continuing
            as my senior honors thesis.
          </p>
          <a class="button-link" href="alma-absorption.html">Open Project Page</a>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card">
          <h3>Tungsten-182 Isotopic Anomalies and Mantle Dynamics</h3>
          <p class="meta">
            Rutgers University · Advisors: Prof. Katherine Bermingham and Prof. Charles-Édouard Boukaré · Jun 2024–May 2025
          </p>
          <p>
            Computational project investigating the origin of tungsten-182 isotopic anomalies using
            geodynamic simulations, Fortran source-code modification, HPC clusters, and Python-based
            analysis of mantle evolution scenarios.
          </p>
